From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yoshisto Yanagisawa <yyanagisawa@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:35:03 -0800
Subject: [M150-LTS] Defer WorkerProcessHandle destruction via DeleteSoon in
 EmbeddedWorkerInstance

Destroying an EmbeddedWorkerInstance (for example, when dropping the
last ServiceWorkerRegistration or ServiceWorkerVersion reference)
previously destroyed WorkerProcessHandle synchronously in
ReleaseProcess(). When the last worker reference on a
RenderProcessHostImpl dropped, DecrementWorkerRefCount() -> Cleanup()
synchronously fired RenderProcessExited() / RenderProcessHostDestroyed()
on the caller's stack, which could tear down callers such as
DedicatedWorkerHost, SharedWorkerHost, or NavigationRequest mid-method.

Defer WorkerProcessHandle destruction via DeleteSoon when `in_dtor_` is
true in EmbeddedWorkerInstance::ReleaseProcess(), and guard
`process_manager_` in ~WorkerProcessHandle() in case the manager is
destroyed before the deferred task runs.

NO_IFTTT = This is to cherry-pick the patch to the M150 branch.

(cherry picked from commit 9bfc328cb45a4395d3563bc557b946078504ca4b)

